1
00:00:14,712 --> 00:00:20,660
Bonjour, Marinette. Tu as un plan pour le week-end ?
Hello, Marinette. Do you have a plan for the weekend?

2
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:26,540
Bonjour, Adrien. Je vais à la mer samedi.
Hello, Adrien. I’m going to the seaside on Saturday.

3
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:29,396
Tu pars avec un ami ?
Are you leaving with a friend?

4
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:35,060
Oui, avec un ami. Nous nageons à la plage.
Yes, with a friend. We’re swimming at the beach.

5
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:39,020
Moi, je vais au parc avec un copain.
I’m going to the park with a friend.

6
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:43,196
Tu joues au tennis, ou tu te reposes ?
Are you playing tennis, or are you resting?

7
00:00:43,296 --> 00:00:48,260
Je joue au tennis samedi, puis je me repose dimanche.
I’m playing tennis on Saturday, then I’m resting on Sunday.

8
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:53,276
Très bien. Bon week-end, Adrien !
Very good. Have a good weekend, Adrien!

9
00:00:53,376 --> 00:00:58,340
Merci, Marinette. À lundi !
Thanks, Marinette. See you Monday!
